# Gmail SMTP credentials for the inquiry form (POST /api/inquiry).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development and fill in the real
# values there. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is the only one that gets
# committed, and it must never contain a real password.
#
# HOW TO GET THE APP PASSWORD
#   1. Turn on 2-Step Verification on the vivir.production@gmail.com account.
#   2. Generate an app password at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   3. Google shows it as four spaced groups ("abcd efgh ijkl mnop"). The
#      password is those 16 characters; the spaces are display only. Pasting it
#      with spaces is fine — the route strips whitespace before authenticating.
#   4. Your normal Google account password will NOT work here. Gmail rejects it
#      for SMTP once 2FA is on.
#
# ON VERCEL
#   Set both values in Project Settings -> Environment Variables (Production,
#   Preview and Development), not in any file in this repo. Redeploy after
#   changing them: environment variables are read at request time by the Node
#   runtime, but a running deployment keeps the values it was built with.
#
# IF EITHER IS MISSING
#   /api/inquiry returns 503 with an operator-facing message and sends nothing.
#   It does not fall back, and it does not write the message anywhere else.

# The mailbox that authenticates to Gmail SMTP and appears in the From header.
GMAIL_USER=vivir.production@gmail.com

# 16-character Google App Password. PLACEHOLDER — replace with the real one in
# .env.local or in Vercel, never here.
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=your-16-char-app-password

# The destination address is NOT an environment variable. It is the exported
# INQUIRY_TO constant in app/api/inquiry/route.ts, so it changes in one place.
